      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits in a narrow valley where Elk Creek meets the South Fork of the New River, surrounded by steep forested slopes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/todd_north_carolina",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 6,000‑year‑old soapstone quarry near Todd shows Native American use long before Europeans arrived.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/todd_north_carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "At its boom, Todd hosted two doctors, a dentist, a bank, seven stores, three mills, and two hotels.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
